\label{rem:continuity-properties-of-loewner-transform} 
Denote by $\funsNodom{\Xpaths}$ the set of continuous functions $W \in \funs{\infty)}$ 
for which the hulls $(\LLoewnerTransform[t](W))_{t \ge 0}$ are generated by a curve. 
When restricted to such drivers, 
the Loewner transform~\eqref{eq:Loewner transform} is not continuous as a map 
to $(\Xpathscl,\dXpaths)$ 
(see~\cite[Lemma~6.3]{Kemppainen:SLE_book}). 
However, the \emph{Loewner inverse transform} 
$\LLoewnerTransform[T]^{-1}(\filling{\gamma[0,T]}) := W \in \funs[\Xpaths]{T]}$, 
given by the driving function $W$ of the curve $\gamma \in \Xpathscl[T]$, is continuous on $\Xpathscl[T]$. 
