\item \label{item:Contraction_principle}
\textnormal{(Contraction principle).} 
If $f \colon X \to Y$ is continuous, then the family $(P^\varepsilon\circ f^{-1})_{\varepsilon > 0}$ 
of pushforward measures satisfies an LDP with good rate function $J \colon Y \to [0,+\infty]$, 
\begin{align*}
